"""Mutations of the rigid body's integration steps (src/game/rigid_body_step.cpp, part 5b) for
../mutfast.py with the step build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_rigid_step.py --models DIR --build build_rigid_step.bat --check check_rigid_step.py

Each should make check_rigid_step.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Left out as equivalent:
the rim's normalisation of `down` (the axle and the planes' line are square, so it is unit), the
toCentre / fromCentre w (the matrix products are affine), StepWheel's centre before Integrate (the
disc has no centre of mass; Collide's is set again before it), the frame's place restored before
Integrate places it again, `sink`'s `* 0.0f` part, the box's empty contact loop when nothing
touches, the frame's Update (the harness's matrices are recomputed), the ignored volume (the test
world does not filter it).

Surviving (2026-10-25, 3 of 311, equivalent): "rim wheel d" (the wheel plane's d only moves the
line's point, which is not used; its direction is the normals' cross product), "rim w" (the axle's
w is the frame matrix's 0), "box out in" (the way out measures the same depth as the contact did,
up to the order of its sum)."""
